Review this final branch state against main. Diff summary: src/auth/permissions.ts now allows support users to approve refunds; src/components/RefundApprovalPanel.tsx exposes the action; tests changed expectations. Base code required admin or finance for refunds over 1000. Changed code:

```ts
// src/auth/permissions.ts
export type Role = 'admin' | 'finance' | 'support' | 'viewer';
export function canApproveRefund(user: { role: Role }, amount: number) {
  if (user.role === 'support') return true;
  return user.role === 'admin' || user.role === 'finance';
}
```

```tsx
// src/components/RefundApprovalPanel.tsx
export function RefundApprovalPanel({ user, refund }: Props) {
  const allowed = canApproveRefund(user, refund.amount);
  return <button disabled={!allowed}>Approve refund</button>;
}
```

```ts
// tests/permissions.test.ts
expect(canApproveRefund({ role: 'support' }, 8000)).toBe(true);
```

Knowledge says support can view refunds but cannot approve high-value refunds without finance review.

Review a React TypeScript hook change. The branch removed cancellation and omitted dependencies:

```ts
// src/hooks/useCustomerRisk.ts
export function useCustomerRisk(customerId: string, includeHistory: boolean) {
  const [risk, setRisk] = useState<Risk | null>(null);
  useEffect(() => {
    setRisk(null);
    fetchRisk(customerId, { includeHistory }).then(setRisk);
  }, [customerId]);
  return risk;
}
```

The old version used an AbortController and included both customerId and includeHistory in dependencies. The app lets the user rapidly switch customers and toggle history.

Review this React change:

```tsx
// src/components/CustomerNote.tsx
type Props = { noteHtml: string; source: 'internal' | 'customer' };
export function CustomerNote({ noteHtml }: Props) {
  return <section className='note' dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{ __html: noteHtml }} />;
}
```

package.json has no sanitizer dependency. Knowledge says customer-originated content must render as text unless explicitly sanitized by a vetted package.

Review this TypeScript change in a dashboard path:

```ts
// src/features/orders/selectors.ts
export function getVisibleOrders(orders: Order[], filter: string) {
  return orders
    .sort((a, b) => b.createdAt.localeCompare(a.createdAt))
    .filter(order => JSON.stringify(order).toLowerCase().includes(filter.toLowerCase()));
}
```

This selector is called during React render. Existing selectors avoid mutating inputs and search only indexed fields.

Review this PR. Source code widened access and test was changed:

```ts
// before
expect(canDeleteUser({ role: 'support' })).toBe(false);
// after
expect(canDeleteUser({ role: 'support' })).toBe(true);
```

```ts
// src/auth/deleteUser.ts
export function canDeleteUser(user: User) {
  return ['admin', 'support'].includes(user.role);
}
```

Product policy says only admins can delete users.

Review this infrastructure change:

```bicep
resource storage 'Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts@2023-01-01' = {
  name: storageName
  location: location
  properties: {
    allowBlobPublicAccess: true
    publicNetworkAccess: 'Enabled'
    minimumTlsVersion: 'TLS1_0'
  }
}
```

Base branch had allowBlobPublicAccess false, publicNetworkAccess Disabled, minimumTlsVersion TLS1_2. Knowledge says demo environments still follow secure defaults.

Review this benign refactor:

```ts
// src/utils/money.ts
export function formatMoney(cents: number, currency = 'USD') {
  return new Intl.NumberFormat('en-US', { style: 'currency', currency }).format(cents / 100);
}
```

The branch replaces duplicated formatting code with this helper and updates call sites. Tests are added for USD and EUR formatting. No security-sensitive files changed.

Review this branch. It adds a new endpoint but no rate limit or auth middleware registration file was changed:

```ts
// src/routes/reportExport.ts
router.post('/exports/report', async (req, res) => {
  const report = await buildReport(req.body.accountId);
  res.json(report);
});
```

Existing protected routes are registered through src/security/protectedRoutes.ts and rate limits through src/security/rateLimits.ts. Neither file appears in changed files.

Review this package-aware change:

```json
